#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/lean-docs-publish.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `lean-html-docs` (`adapters/paper/lean/lean-docs-build.sh --lake-root <pkg> --lib <Lib>`). Reads the SOURCE, the folio's Lake packages. Refuses while another lake/lean process holds `.lake/`, refuses over a restored tree with no traces, checks or restores the warm cache, enables the sentinel-commented doc-gen4 require for this build only, then `lake -R -Kenv=dev build <Lib>:docs`. Output: `<pkg>/.lake/build/doc-data` (the per-module declaration data the viewer is made from) and `<pkg>/.lake/build/doc` (the static HTML, kept only as the fallback): working directories, not yet anything a site reads."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/lean-docs-publish.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `lean-kg-publish` (`adapters/paper/lean/lean-kg-publish.ts --doc-data <pkg>/.lake/build/doc-data --site <checkout> --route <store path> --no-rail`) writes the viewer page and its `data/` shards into the mounted store's path (the folio's declared `lean` graph, e.g. `lean/`), then `bun folio-assistant/cat-harness-tools/scripts/branch-store.ts push --id <id>`. The store is tip-keyed: the branch tip IS the current render, with a root `manifest.json` (`state-manifest/v1`); the push splices onto the tip and never forces. The render is never committed to the folio's main."
msgstr ""

